MANUAL — per the delegation's checklist, against ACCESSIBILITY.md #4/#9/#12
1. Converted sliders (healthcare cost/inflation, portfolio, inflation rate,
   spending-decline rate*, investment-return, spending-phase multipliers —
   tested healthcare-monthly-cost, portfolio-slider, inflation-rate-slider,
   phase-0/1-multiplier directly; *spending-decline-slider is template-
   conditional on SpendingPhaseConfig.Enabled=false and didn't render on
   this fixture — same JS/markup pattern verified on the other 5, so not a
   gap):
   - Accessible name resolves via `label[for=]` → visible range id in every
     case (e.g. "Monthly Cost", confirmed live via
     `document.querySelector('label[for="healthcare-monthly-cost-<id>"]')`).
   - Visible range carries no `name=` (mirror-only); role is the native
     range/slider; `aria-valuetext` present at load and EXACT (portfolio
     "$2,437,512" for stored 2437512.34; healthcare "$1,655" for 1655.30;
     phase multiplier "93%" for 0.93) — not the step-snapped display.
   - Keyboard operation (ArrowRight, End tested) updates `aria-valuetext`
     live via the generalized `syncQuickAdjustAriaValueTexts` path (not
     only on mouse drag): healthcare $1,655→$1,700→$3,000 (End→max),
     portfolio $2,437,512→$2,500,000, phases 100%→105%/93%→100%.
   - Keyboard operation saves the exact arrowed-to value: after one
     ArrowRight + Tab-blur, `/whatif/healthcare/<id>` PUT fired and the
     saved `current_monthly_cost` became exactly 1700 (hidden field also
     read 1700) — not silently re-snapped. A native `<input type=range>`
     fires `change` on every arrow keystroke (browser behavior, not a WS1
     mechanism), so the debounced `hx-trigger="change delay:500ms"` PUT
     fired after the single keystroke too — this is unchanged native range
     behavior, present identically on master's un-mirrored slider (the
     control being fired is different, the per-keystroke-fires-change fact
     is not), so NOT a WS1-introduced regression.
   - Hidden canonical inputs: confirmed via a real Tab sequence starting
     from the visible range — focus moves range→range→range→range→number→
     number, the four interleaved `type=hidden` siblings are never focused
     (DOM `.tabIndex` reads 0 but `type=hidden` is unconditionally excluded
     from the focus order per browser behavior, confirmed empirically, not
     just asserted).
   - Duplicate id claim: `healthcare-pre-medicare-inflation-<id>` is
     authored at two template sites (line ~109 `{{else if ne
     .CurrentCoverage "medicare"}}` under the non-employer/non-medicare
     branch, and line ~148 under `{{if eq .CurrentCoverage
     "employer"}}{{if gt .EmployerCoverageYears 0}}`) — mutually exclusive
     conditions (employer vs. not-employer-and-not-medicare). Live DOM scan
     on the ACA fixture person confirms zero duplicate ids anywhere on the
     page. Confirmed only one renders, per the delegation's ask.
2. Number inputs with `step="any"`: spin/Arrow behavior tested on
   state-income-tax-rate (was step 0.05), taxable-cost-basis (was step
   1000), ss-cola-rate (was step 0.1), property-tax-inflation (was step
   0.1) — ArrowUp on each steps by exactly 1.0 (HTML default step for
   step="any"). USABILITY OBSERVATION (not a WCAG failure — the field
   remains keyboard-operable, #9 is met; WCAG 2.2 AA and ACCESSIBILITY.md
   are both silent on step granularity): state_income_tax_rate and
   ss_cola_rate arrows are now ~10–20x coarser (0.05/0.1→1); several
   dollar fields (care_monthly_cost step 50, aca_premium_credit step 100,
   taxable_cost_basis step 1000) are now far FINER via arrows (step 1),
   meaning reaching a six-figure cost-basis by arrow key alone takes many
   more presses than before. Typing a value directly is unaffected either
   way. Validity messages remain sane: an out-of-range entry (-5 on cost
   basis) still reports `rangeUnderflow` with message "Value must be
   greater than or equal to 0."; the exact off-grid fixture value
   (276146.86) round-trips as valid.
3. Quick Adjust drawer healthcare mirrors (`web/templates/components/
   whatif/quick-adjust.html`, e.g. `#qa-healthcare-monthly-cost-<id>`):
   labelled correctly (`label[for=]` resolves to "Monthly Cost"), BUT they
   never carry `aria-valuetext` — not at load, and never synced, because
   `syncQuickAdjustAriaValueTexts` only ever sets `aria-valuetext` on a
   control that ALREADY has the attribute
   (`if (!control.hasAttribute('aria-valuetext')) return;`), and this
   template's mirror ranges were never authored with a starting one.
   Confirmed live: after opening Quick Adjust and pressing ArrowRight on
   the drawer's own healthcare-cost slider, the drawer control still has
   `aria-valuetext: null` while the primary in-card slider's
   `aria-valuetext` correctly updated to "$1,750" from the same keystroke.
   `quick-adjust.html` is NOT in WS1.1.diff's file list (11 files touched:
   the test file, render.go, two JS files, and 7 `web/templates/components/
   whatif/*.html` files — quick-adjust.html is not among them) — this gap
   is PRE-EXISTING and unchanged by this task in either direction (master's
   drawer slider had the identical absence). OBSERVATION, not a FAIL, per
   the git-diff-master attribution rule — but worth flagging for the
   backlog: the WS1 code comment on `syncQuickAdjustAriaValueTexts` claims
   the mechanism "covers the primary in-card slider AND its Quick Adjust
   mirror alike", which is not true for the healthcare keys' QA-drawer
   controls specifically (they were never opted in), so the comment
   overclaims for this instance — a good V3/backlog candidate, not a WS1
   scope failure since the file is untouched.
   Also observed for completeness: `investment-return-slider` was never
   given an `aria-valuetext` either (deliberate per its own code comment —
   0 has non-numeric meaning "use allocation" with no single-string
   format) — unchanged from master, not a regression.
4. axe-core (both themes, all disclosures + Quick Adjust open) found no
